From a3835e143417839aa822f05f9f3cec0e69b12575 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (via chat)" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 23:34:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix: dropdown menu was transparent with no z-index,
 letting hero slider show through
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

.slicknav_nav had background: rgba(0,0,0,0) (fully transparent) and
z-index: auto, while .hero-slider explicitly sets z-index: 1 — so the
rotating hero carousel was painting on top of the see-through dropdown,
creating an overlapping, unreadable mess of both sets of text.

Fix: give the dropdown a solid background (var(--ink-900), matching
the site's dark theme) and z-index: 500 so it properly sits above the
hero slider instead of blending with it.

Verified live: dropdown is now solid and readable immediately on open
and after 2s+ of carousel auto-rotation behind it. All 5 menu links
confirmed present and intact.
---
 public/css/design-system.css | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/public/css/design-system.css b/public/css/design-system.css
index 39b9e98..aca8f0d 100644
--- a/public/css/design-system.css
+++ b/public/css/design-system.css
@@ -361,6 +361,9 @@ select:focus-visible, textarea:focus-visible {
   left: 0 !important;
   right: 0 !important;
   width: auto !important;
+  background: var(--ink-900) !important;  /* was fully transparent — hero slider (z-index:1) was */
+  z-index: 500 !important;                /* showing straight through it */
+  box-shadow: var(--shadow);
 }
 
 /* Modal close button */
